  "_doc": "DISPLAYED vs CALCULATED classification for the 101 money columns in plan.json (92 CENTS + 9 NUM6). DISPLAYED = an amount a person sees, pays, is charged or is refunded; it is settled in the currency's smallest payable unit and never needs to be finer. CALCULATED = an amount derived by arithmetic (division, per-unit rate, roll-up, average) that is an INPUT to further arithmetic before anyone sees it; sub-cent resolution in these is real signal, not noise. 'boundary' marks columns whose role is arguable and which the report prints separately.",
